// Recoveries under the derived compute budget (design record 079). Each line is an item and ";". A line
// that does not match is skipped up to its ";" and recovered, which builds a syntax error. The rule
// line is called at two places: the first alternative of doc fails after the line, where no "!"
// follows, the store of the memo takes the entries of the errors recovered in the line, and the
// second call reuses the result and records its list of errors.

package recover

@start
rule doc = (line "!" / line)* $$
rule line = (item ";") #recover(skip=[^;]* ";")
rule item = word ("=" word)? ws
rule word = [a-z]+
rule ws = " "*
